      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© The Author(s) 2015 Reprints and permissions: sagepub.co.uk/journalsPermissions.nav.",
        "AbstractText": "Isolated single coronary artery is an extremely rare anomaly with an incidence of 0.024% to 0.066% which may be associated with other congenital anomalies. This report describes a 50-year-old woman who was referred with recurrent chest discomfort and was diagnosed with anomalous origin of the right coronary artery from the left circumflex coronary artery."
